---
// Draft, written from what this website does today (no forms, analytics or cookies; hosted on Cloudflare Pages).
// Facts confirmed by the client on 2026-11-17 (Microsoft 365, 2 and 7 years). The client's lawyer must review it before launch.
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro';
const email = 'hr@crescoprime.com';
---
<Legal title="Privacy policy" description="How Cresco Prime LLC collects, uses and protects personal information on crescoprime.com and when you contact us.">
  <p>Last updated: November 17, 2026.</p>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal information Cresco Prime LLC (&ldquo;Cresco Prime&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;,
    &ldquo;us&rdquo;) collects when you visit crescoprime.com or get in touch with us, how we use it, and the choices
    you have. If you become a client, our written agreement with you also covers how we handle the data you give us
    for the work.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Cresco Prime LLC is an IT services and consulting company based in Frisco, Texas, United States. We are
    responsible for the personal information described in this policy. You can reach us at{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p><strong>When you browse this website.</strong> The site has no forms, no accounts, no analytics and no advertising trackers, and we set no cookies.</p>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider, Cloudflare, receives the technical details that every website receives when a browser asks
    for a page: your IP address, your browser and device type, the page you asked for and the time. Cloudflare uses
    them to deliver the site and to protect it from attacks, and it may set a strictly necessary security cookie to
    tell people apart from automated traffic.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your browser also keeps one temporary note in its session storage so the animation between pages can finish. The
    note holds no personal information, never leaves your device and disappears when you close the tab.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>When you contact us.</strong> If you email us, message us on WhatsApp, or write to us on LinkedIn or
    Instagram, we receive what you send: usually your name, your email address or phone number, your company and your
    message. On WhatsApp we also see your profile name.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to you and discuss the work you ask about.</li>
    <li>To prepare proposals and, if you become a client, to deliver and invoice the work.</li>
    <li>To keep this website running and secure.</li>
    <li>To meet our legal, tax and accounting obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information, share it for advertising, or use it to make automated decisions about you.</p>

  <h2>Our legal bases (visitors in the EU and UK)</h2>
  <p>
    We use your information because we have a legitimate interest in answering enquiries and running a secure website,
    because you asked us to take steps before a contract or we have a contract with you, or because the law requires
    it. Where we rely on legitimate interests, you can object at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal information only with providers that help us run the business, under their own privacy and security terms:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Cloudflare, Inc., which hosts and protects this website.</li>
    <li>Microsoft Corporation, whose Microsoft 365 service carries our email.</li>
    <li>WhatsApp (Meta Platforms), LinkedIn and Instagram, when you choose to message us there. Their own privacy policies apply to those conversations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information when the law requires it, or to protect our rights or someone&rsquo;s safety. If
    Cresco Prime is ever merged or sold, the information may pass to the new owner, who must keep this policy&rsquo;s
    promises.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    We are based in the United States, and our providers may process data in the United States and other countries.
    When personal information from the EU or the UK is transferred, we rely on safeguards such as the Standard
    Contractual Clauses our providers offer.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Enquiries that do not lead to work: up to 2 years after our last contact, then deleted.</li>
    <li>Client records: for the length of the engagement, plus up to 7 years, the time tax and accounting law requires.</li>
    <li>Website logs: kept by Cloudflare for its own limited period.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we protect it</h2>
  <p>
    We protect the information we hold with access controls, multi-factor authentication and encrypted connections. No
    system is perfectly secure, so we cannot promise absolute security, but we will tell you without undue delay if a
    breach affects your information.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>know what personal information we hold about you and get a copy;</li>
    <li>have it corrected or deleted;</li>
    <li>object to or restrict how we use it;</li>
    <li>receive it in a format you can take elsewhere.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Residents of several US states have similar rights under state privacy laws. To use any of these rights, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We will answer within 30 days and will not treat you differently for
    asking. If you are in the EU or the UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is for businesses and is not aimed at children under 16. We do not knowingly collect their
    information. If you think a child has sent us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to LinkedIn, Instagram and WhatsApp. Those services decide how they handle your information, so
    please read their privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when our practices change, for example if we add a contact form or analytics, and we will
    change the date at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Cresco Prime LLC, Frisco, Texas, United States. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
